[{:seon.task/name "the-scenarios-measure-real-agents"
  :seon.task/plan "Found by the first DeepSeek runs (2026-10-21, `bin/check e2e scenario <k> model`): the scenarios were written against the scripted model, and three things hid behind it.
- A spec with no `:plan` gets `seon.fixtures/decls`' default, which cites `app.m/a`, the task's own name, as if it were a var (`hairy`'s specs a and b). The real agents capped through two refinements (24 calls, 69k tokens) looking for code the plan never named. Correct: the default plan cites the vars the task's proof calls (read from the proof's form with `seon.ref`'s name rule or the reader), so a spec with no plan still cites what to change.
- In model mode, `newns`' verdict asserts the scripted reply's extra content (a dynamic `*depth*`, `ops`, `syms`) that its plan never asks for; the real agent did what the plan asked (proof green, merged) and the scenario still failed. Correct: a model-mode verdict asserts what the plan and proofs ask (the merged program passes the task's proofs and the plan's stated behaviour), and the scripted-only details stay in scripted mode.
- `seon.e2e/numbers`' `:turns-per-merged-task` averages the turns of `:merged` attempts, which are merge tasks with 0 turns, so it always reads 0. Correct: turns per task that reached main, counting the work attempts of each merged task.
Write the three proofs first in `test/seon/e2e_test.clj` and watch them fail; then rerun `scenario hairy model` and `scenario newns model` (DeepSeek, `SEON_PROFILE` not needed: `model` selects the provider; the key is `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` in `~/src/seon-jolt/.env`) and report calls and tokens against the first run's (hairy 24 calls / 69k tokens, failed; newns 2 calls, verdict failed)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.e2e-test/a-default-plan-cites-the-vars-its-proof-calls
                      seon.e2e-test/a-model-run-is-judged-by-what-the-plan-asks
                      seon.e2e-test/turns-count-the-work-attempts}}]
